          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: поломка",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "поломка (polómka) — \"a breakdown, a fault\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Из-за поломки мы приехали домой поздно. Iz-za polómki my priyékhali domóy pózdno. Because of the breakdown we got home late."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine. Built on поломать — to break."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "поломка (polómka) is built on поломать 'to break', from ломать 'to break'; EtymDB lists ломать without a deeper source."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
